# LOCAL DEPLOYMENT TOOLING, ignored rather than committed, and the reason is not that it
# is scratch work.
#
# All three were written against ONE host and two named radios — a hardcoded nginx
# container, a hardcoded gateway address, hardcoded LAN ranges, a hardcoded domain and
# two hardcoded radio names. That is no use to anyone else forking this, and it is also
# why they cannot be published: this fork's origin is PUBLIC, and those files are a
# description of a private network.
#
# What they should be is a generator: ask what it cannot work out, derive the rest (the
# gateway already answers GET /devices with every radio it holds and its alias, so the
# hostnames follow from the gateway rather than from a list someone typed), and emit a
# recommended config. Until they are that, they stay on the machine they were written
# for. Not urgent — Peter, 2026-10-31.
deploy.sh
check.sh
nginx/
